#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: Kansas
#> pause: 40
#> must: Kansas
#> must: # command:  sed  -f
#> not: Montana
#> not: Alabama
#> source: /an/!d; /as/!d
# 19. Lines that match AAA and BBB, in any order. Pement: sed '/AAA/!d; /BBB/!d'
# Each !d deletes a line that lacks one of the words, so only lines with both
# survive: Kansas has both "an" and "as"; the others have one at most. For
# "either" (grep -E 'AAA|BBB') the GNU form is  /AAA\|BBB/!d
# Try: /an.*as/!d  demands the order too; Kansas still passes.
/an/!d; /as/!d

#DATA
Alabama
Alaska
Iowa
Kansas
Montana
